    <dcterms:provenance xml:lang="en">&lt;p&gt;**For both the present painting (SK-A-1247) and its pendant (SK-A-1246)**&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&#8230;; collection Jan van de Poll (1721-1801), Amsterdam;{RANH, ARS, IS, inv. no. 168, no. 302 (14 April 1884).} his grandson Jan van de Poll (1777-1858), Amsterdam, 1802 (stored with other family portraits in his aunt&#8217;s house, Herengracht 479 in Amsterdam); his son Jan Stanislaus Robert van de Poll (1805-88), Arnhem (stored with 25 other family portraits in his sister-in-law&#8217;s house, Herengracht 450 in Amsterdam); by whom donated to the museum together with 34 other family portraits, as _&lt;em&gt;Portrait of Nicolaes Hasselaer&lt;/em&gt;_ and _&lt;em&gt;Portrait of a Woman&lt;/em&gt;_, November 1885{RANH, ARS, IS, inv. 164, no. 299 (30 December 1884); RANH, ARS, Kop, inv. 289, pp. 62-68, no. 154 (19 November 1885).}&lt;/p&gt;</dcterms:provenance>
